{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwZhNunppH1YYPKgyXHT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a `test:checkout` script to `package.json`, but I couldn't run it because `node_modules` isn't installed. Nothing has been tested yet.\n\n```json\n\"test:checkout\": \"vitest run src/cart.test.js -t \\\"^cart checkout \\\"\"\n```\n\n**How it works:** Vitest's `-t` option checks a regular expression against each test's full name, which is its block names and test name joined by spaces. The cart checkout tests are named like `cart checkout charges the total`, so `^cart checkout ` matches them. Any test added to that block later will start with the same prefix, so it gets picked up too.\n\n**What it leaves out:**\n- `wishlist checkout …` doesn't start with `cart`, so the `^` excludes it.\n- `cart items …` doesn't match the `checkout` part.\n- The space at the end stops it from matching a future sibling block with a longer name, such as `checkoutSummary`.\n\nThe escaped double quotes work in both cmd and POSIX shells, so the script runs on Windows too.\n\nTo confirm it, run `npm install` and then `npm run test:checkout`. You should see exactly 2 tests run: \"charges the total\" and \"rejects an empty cart\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":602,"cache_read_input_tokens":23190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":602},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"337c47fa-8eec-4cd2-ba50-3970bdecaa4e","uuid":"1b5031d0-f111-47e9-ac42-ba34139c63e1","timestamp":"2026-10-12T02:36:22.836Z","request_id":"req_011CfwZhNefSHqkMiuEW5Jku"}
